  "noMusicReason": "Standing rule (2026-08-24 user directive): reels ship voice + SFX only, no music bed by default. Set plan[\"music\"] = true (or a full music object) to opt this reel back into a bed.",
  "script": "A leaker just flipped everything you thought you knew about the iPhone 18 Pro's colors.\n\nWhat nobody's flagging yet: Apple reveals the actual lineup in just 7 days.\n\nUntil this week, the accepted story was 4 colors: dark cherry, silver, dark gray, and light blue.\n\nNow a leaker who tracks Apple's supply chain says that list is wrong.\n\nTheir replacement is just 3 colors: dark cherry, sky blue, and black.\n\nSilver was the color everyone expected.\n\nIt's reportedly gone.\n\nThey say they've found zero evidence of it in China's supply chain.\n\nAnd 2 separate outlets reported that exact claim, same day.\n\nBut a second leak, working from actual CAD drawings, disagrees completely.\n\nIt keeps silver alive, and pairs a dark gray with a light blue instead of black.\n\nSo out of those 4 original colors, only 1 survives both leaks.\n\nThat one's a deep, wine-toned dark cherry, replacing last year's cosmic orange.\n\nMeaning, the rest of this story is currently contradicted.\n\nThat's usually a sign the lineup isn't locked yet inside Apple, and even people with real access are still guessing this close to launch.\n\nThat's real, official, and just days away, on September 9th.\n\nSo remember what nobody flagged: which list do you think actually survives?",
